<BODY STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif">

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: center">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: right"><B>Exhibit 99.1</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: center">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-left: 40pt; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: left"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B><IMG SRC="ex99-1_001.jpg" ALT="" STYLE="height: 92px; width: 164px"></B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="text-align: center; font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>&nbsp;</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>VERB
Announces Stockholder Approved Reverse Split</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="text-align: center; font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; background-color: white"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>&nbsp;</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; background-color: white"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>Stockholders
Vote Overwhelmingly (84.16%) in Favor of Reverse Stock Split</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="text-align: center; font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; background-color: white"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>&nbsp;</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify; background-color: white"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">NEWPORT
BEACH, Calif. and SALT LAKE CITY, April 18, 2023 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) &mdash; <B><U>Verb Technology Company, Inc.</U> (Nasdaq: VERB) </B>(&ldquo;VERB&rdquo;
or the &ldquo;Company&rdquo;), the leader in interactive video-based sales-enablement applications, including <U>MARKET.live,</U> its
livestream social shopping platform, today announced that its Board of Directors authorized the stockholder approved 1-for-40 reverse
stock split of its common stock shares and that the common stock shares will begin trading on a split-adjusted basis at the commencement
of trading April 19, 2023. The Company&rsquo;s shares will continue to trade on the Nasdaq Capital Market under the same symbol &ldquo;VERB&rdquo;
with a new CUSIP number, 92337U203.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify; background-color: white; color: #212529"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify; background-color: white; color: #212529"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">As
set forth in the current report on Form 8-K filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission (the &ldquo;SEC&rdquo;), on April 14, 2023,
the Company, held a special meeting of stockholders (the &ldquo;Special Meeting&rdquo;) to vote on four Proposals, including Proposal
number 2 which was to authorize the board of directors to effect a reverse stock split of the outstanding shares of common stock within
one (1) year of April 10, 2023, at a specific ratio within a range of one-for-five (1-for-5) to a maximum of a one-for-forty (1-for-40).</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify; background-color: white; color: #212529"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt; background-color: white; color: #212529"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Present
virtually at the Special Meeting, or represented by valid proxy and entitled to vote as of the record date for the Special Meeting, were
a total of 77,367,918 shares of the Company&rsquo;s common stock, out of a total of 153,610,152 shares of common stock issued and outstanding
and entitled to vote, and the one share of the Company&rsquo;s Series B Preferred Stock (the &ldquo;Preferred Stock&rdquo;) that was
issued and outstanding. With respect to the vote authorizing the reverse split, the Preferred Stock could only cast votes in the same
exact proportion as the common stockholders voted their shares at the Special Meeting, both For and Against. Accordingly, the votes of
the Preferred Stock could not change the outcome of the vote of the common stockholders, only amplify it.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; background-color: white; color: #212529"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; background-color: white; color: #212529"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
stockholders voted overwhelmingly in favor of authorizing the Company&rsquo;s board of directors to institute a reverse stock split,
as set forth in greater specificity in the Company&rsquo;s April 14, 2023 Form 8-K.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt; background-color: white; color: #212529"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>


<!-- Field: Page; Sequence: 1 -->
    <DIV STYLE="margin-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: Black 1.5pt solid"><TABLE CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" STYLE="border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 10pt"><TR STYLE="vertical-align: top; text-align: left"><TD STYLE="width: 100%">&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE></DIV>
    <DIV STYLE="break-before: page; margin-top: 6pt"><TABLE CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" STYLE="border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 10pt"><TR STYLE="vertical-align: top; text-align: left"><TD STYLE="text-align: center; width: 100%">&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE></DIV>
    <!-- Field: /Page -->

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; color: #212529"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify; background-color: white; color: #212529"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Following
the vote of stockholders at the Company&rsquo;s Special Meeting, the Board of Directors approved a 1-for-40 reverse stock split of the
Company&rsquo;s issued and outstanding shares of common stock, par value $0.0001 per share. Every 40 shares of the Company&rsquo;s issued
and outstanding common stock will automatically convert into one share of common stock without any change to the par value of $0.0001
per share. The amount of common stock outstanding will be reduced from approximately 153.6 million shares to approximately 3.8 million
shares. Proportional adjustments will be made to the number of shares of common stock issuable upon exercise of the Company&rsquo;s outstanding
stock options and warrants, as well as the applicable exercise price.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; background-color: white; color: #212529"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="text-align: justify; font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; background-color: white; color: #212529"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Company expects that the stockholder approved reverse stock split will increase the market price per share of the Company&rsquo;s common
stock, bringing the Company into compliance with The Nasdaq Capital Market&rsquo;s $1.00 minimum bid price listing requirement.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; background-color: white; color: #212529"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt; background-color: white; color: #212529"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&ldquo;I
am hopeful that our stockholders&rsquo; decision with regard to the reverse split serves not only to allow the Company to regain compliance
with Nasdaq&rsquo;s listing requirements, but also as another tool in our arsenal as we combat the apparent naked short selling of our
shares that may have artificially depressed our share price leading to this action we have taken today,&rdquo; states VERB&rsquo;s CEO,
Rory J. Cutaia. &ldquo;We intend to provide an update to all stockholders this week on the actions we have recently taken following the
extensive, month&rsquo;s long compilation and analysis of the evidence produced by our experts.&rdquo;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; background-color: white; color: #212529"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt; background-color: white; color: #212529"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Registered
stockholders holding pre-split shares of the Company&rsquo;s common stock are not required to take any action to receive post-split shares.
Stockholders owning shares via a broker, bank, trust or other nominee will have their positions automatically adjusted to reflect the
reverse stock split, and will not be required to take any action in connection with the reverse stock split.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; background-color: white; color: #212529"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt; background-color: white; color: #212529"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">No
fractional shares will be issued in connection with the reverse stock split. Any fractional shares created as a result of the reverse
stock split will be rounded up to the nearest whole share for each stockholder. The reverse stock split impacts all holders of VERB&rsquo;s
common stock proportionally and will not impact stockholders&rsquo; percentage of ownership of common stock (except as to rounding-up
changes).</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; background-color: white; color: #212529"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify; background-color: white; color: #212529"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Additional
information regarding the reverse stock split is available on the Form 8-K filed April 14, 2023, as well as in the Company&rsquo;s definitive
proxy statement (Form DEF 14A) filed with the SEC on February 28, 2023. Any additional questions can be directed to the Company&rsquo;s
transfer agent, VStock Transfer, at (212) 826-8436 or www.vstocktransfer.com.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; background-color: white; color: #212529"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>&nbsp;</B></FONT></P>


